  7623→
  7624→      - title: "UI Design System"
  7625→        slug: ui-design-system
  7626→        type: feature
  7627→        parent: "@web-ui"
  7628→        description: |
  7629→          Port imgen's design token architecture into kspec's Tailwind-based web UI.
  7630→          Map oklch color tokens, spacing, radii, z-index, typography, and animation
  7631→          keyframes as Tailwind theme extensions. Establish consistent visual language
  7632→          across all views.
  7633→        acceptance_criteria:
  7634→          - id: ac-1
  7635→            given: |
  7636→              The web UI app.css file
  7637→            when: |
  7638→              imgen token-contract.css values are mapped as Tailwind @theme inline extensions
  7639→            then: |
  7640→              All 16 color tokens, 4 radii, 7 spacing, 7 z-index, and 3 font families
  7641→              are available as Tailwind utility classes (e.g. bg-design-surface, border-design-border)
  7642→          - id: ac-2
  7643→            given: |
  7644→              A component using design tokens
  7645→            when: |
  7646→              The dark theme tokens are applied
  7647→            then: |
  7648→              oklch colors render correctly and status colors (pending=amber, in_progress=orange,
  7649→              pending_review=blue, needs_work=yellow, completed=emerald, blocked=red, cancelled=gray)
  7650→              are visually distinct
  7651→          - id: ac-3
  7652→            given: |
  7653→              A view with loading states
  7654→            when: |
  7655→              Content is loading
  7656→            then: |
  7657→              Shimmer animation plays on skeleton elements, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion
  7658→          - id: ac-4
  7659→            given: |
  7660→              An active agent task card
  7661→            when: |
  7662→              The agent is working
  7663→            then: |
  7664→              Breathing/pulse animation plays on the card border, gated behind prefers-reduced-motion
  7665→
  7666→      - title: "App Shell and Navigation"
  7667→        slug: ui-app-shell
  7668→        type: feature
  7669→        parent: "@web-ui"
  7670→        description: |
  7671→          Restructure the web UI layout with collapsible sidebar navigation, header bar
  7672→          with command palette and connection status, and grouped navigation sections.
  7673→          Preserve existing functionality during migration.
  7674→        acceptance_criteria:
  7675→          - id: ac-1
  7676→            given: |
  7677→              The web UI loaded in daemon mode
  7678→            when: |
  7679→              The app shell renders
  7680→            then: |
  7681→              A collapsible sidebar shows grouped navigation: Work (Dashboard, Tasks, Agents, Sessions),
  7682→              Specs (Specs, Plans, Validate), Capture (Inbox, Observations, Triage),
  7683→              Config (Workflows, Settings)
  7684→          - id: ac-2
  7685→            given: |
  7686→              Sidebar navigation items
  7687→            when: |
  7688→              Items have actionable counts (inbox items, unresolved observations, pending review tasks)
  7689→            then: |
  7690→              Badge counts display next to the relevant nav items
  7691→          - id: ac-3
  7692→            given: |
  7693→              The /items route
  7694→            when: |
  7695→              A user navigates to /items
  7696→            then: |
  7697→              They are redirected to /specs preserving any query parameters
  7698→          - id: ac-4
  7699→            given: |
  7700→              The Observations nav item
  7701→            when: |
  7702→              There are zero unresolved observations
  7703→            then: |
  7704→              The nav item is still visible (not hidden)
  7705→
  7706→      - title: "Task Board (Kanban)"
  7707→        slug: ui-task-board
  7708→        type: feature
  7709→        parent: "@web-ui"
  7710→        description: |
  7711→          Kanban-style task board with columns mapping to kspec task states.
  7712→          Active Fleet row shows currently running agent work with live output.
  7713→          Task cards show key metadata, clicking opens detail modal.
  7714→          Not drag-and-drop — tasks transition via agents/CLI.
  7715→        acceptance_criteria:
  7716→          - id: ac-1
  7717→            given: |
  7718→              Tasks in various states
  7719→            when: |
  7720→              The task board renders
  7721→            then: |
  7722→              Tasks are distributed into columns: Backlog (pending, manual_only/unassessed),
  7723→              Ready (pending, eligible), In Progress (in_progress, needs_work),
  7724→              Review (pending_review), Done (completed recent), with blocked and cancelled
  7725→              handled as sections/indicators
  7726→          - id: ac-2
  7727→            given: |
  7728→              A task card on the board
  7729→            when: |
  7730→              The card renders
  7731→            then: |
  7732→              It shows priority badge, tag chips, title, slug (mono), spec ref link,
  7733→              and metadata footer (notes count, dependency count, age)
  7734→          - id: ac-3
  7735→            given: |
  7736→              A task card
  7737→            when: |
  7738→              The user clicks it
  7739→            then: |
  7740→              A detail modal opens showing full task info: title, description, status,
  7741→              priority, type, spec ref, tags, dependencies, blocked-by, notes, todos,
  7742→              automation status, VCS info (branch, PR link), plan ref, session link
  7743→          - id: ac-4
  7744→            given: |
  7745→              Agents actively working on tasks (dispatch running)
  7746→            when: |
  7747→              The task board renders
  7748→            then: |
  7749→              An Active Fleet row appears at the top showing cards with task title,
  7750→              agent name, elapsed time with pulse indicator, and last few lines of output
  7751→          - id: ac-5
  7752→            given: |
  7753→              The task board with WebSocket connected
  7754→            when: |
  7755→              A task state changes
  7756→            then: |
  7757→              The board updates in real-time without page refresh
  7758→          - id: ac-6
  7759→            given: |
  7760→              The task detail modal in daemon mode
  7761→            when: |
  7762→              The user clicks action buttons (Start, Submit, Complete, Block, Add Note)
  7763→            then: |
  7764→              The corresponding task transition or mutation is executed via API
  7765→
  7766→      - title: "Session Stream View"
  7767→        slug: ui-session-stream
  7768→        type: feature
  7769→        parent: "@web-ui"
  7770→        description: |
  7771→          View for watching agent work — both historical and live. Renders structured
  7772→          session events (messages, tool calls, thinking blocks) from events.jsonl.
  7773→          Live sessions show streaming text with periodic structured refresh.
  7774→        acceptance_criteria:
  7775→          - id: ac-1
  7776→            given: |
  7777→              A completed session with events.jsonl
  7778→            when: |
  7779→              The user navigates to /sessions/:id
  7780→            then: |
  7781→              The session events render as structured blocks: agent messages (markdown),
  7782→              tool calls (collapsible with icon, input/output, timing), and thinking blocks
  7783→              (collapsed by default, expandable)
  7784→          - id: ac-2
  7785→            given: |
  7786→              An active session with streaming output
  7787→            when: |
  7788→              The user views the session
  7789→            then: |
  7790→              Live text streams in real-time via agent_text_chunk WebSocket events,
  7791→              with periodic structured refresh from events.jsonl
  7792→          - id: ac-3
  7793→            given: |
  7794→              The session stream view
  7795→            when: |
  7796→              New content arrives while auto-scrolling
  7797→            then: |
  7798→              The view auto-scrolls to follow new content, pauses when user scrolls up
  7799→              (>100px from bottom), and resumes when scrolled back. A "jump to bottom"
  7800→              button appears when paused.
  7801→          - id: ac-4
  7802→            given: |
  7803→              The session stream view
  7804→            when: |
  7805→              A session context panel is shown on the left
  7806→            then: |
  7807→              It displays session metadata, spec context with AC checklist,
  7808→              files changed during session, and budget info
  7809→
  7810→      - title: "Agent and Dispatch View"
  7811→        slug: ui-agent-dispatch
  7812→        type: feature
  7813→        parent: "@web-ui"
  7814→        description: |
  7815→          View showing agent definitions, dispatch status (running/stopped),
  7816→          and active invocations with links to session streams.
